From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] phy: mediatek: mipi-dsi: add MT6897

Add the D-PHY of MT6897, from mtk_mipi_tx_pll_prepare_mt6897() and
mtk_mipi_tx_dphy_lane_config_mt6897() of the MediaTek driver. The
driving strength setting with DEM_EN comes from the driver of the Lenovo
TB375FC, and is in its stock module.

The bootloader trims the lanes and nothing else knows the values, so
probe saves them and power on writes them back, like the vendor does.
The enable and disable of the PLL sleep, so they are prepare and
unprepare here. A PLL that is on stays as it is, also like the vendor:
this block has no power domain, and it can still run from the
bootloader.

The vendor picks the divider from the nominal rate of the panel (1004
Mbps for one whose real rate is 998.137 Mbps), so the divider of 2
starts a little below 1 Gbps here.
---
 drivers/phy/mediatek/Makefile                 |   1 +
 .../phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-mipi-dsi-mt6897.c    | 239 ++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-mipi-dsi.c       |   7 +
 drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-mipi-dsi.h       |   5 +
 4 files changed, 252 insertions(+)

